{"name":"Chinotto","hex":"#554747","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Chinotto (drink)","blocks":[{"text":"Chinotto is a carbonated soft drink produced from the juice of the fruit of the myrtle-leaved orange tree. The beverage is dark in color. Its appearance is similar to that of cola, but it is not as sweet, having a bittersweet taste."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Citrus_myrtifolia_2.jpg/330px-Citrus_myrtifolia_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinotto_(drink)","wikidata":"Q950733"},{"title":"Citrus myrtifolia","blocks":[{"text":"Citrus myrtifolia (chinotto), the myrtle-leaved orange tree, is a species of Citrus with foliage similar to that of the common myrtle. It is a compact tree with small leaves and no thorns which grows to a height of three metres (10 ft) and can be found in Malta, Libya, the south of France, and Italy (primarily in Liguria, typically Savona, and also in Tuscany, Sicily, and Calabria)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Citrus_myrtifolia_2.jpg/330px-Citrus_myrtifolia_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citrus_myrtifolia","wikidata":"Q1074438"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Paris_-_Cour_Saint-%C3%89milion_-_20130801_%281%29.jpg/500px-Paris_-_Cour_Saint-%C3%89milion_-_20130801_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Paris_-_Cour_Saint-%C3%89milion_-_20130801_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Paris_-_Cour_Saint-%C3%89milion_-_20130801_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Paris_-_Cour_Saint-%C3%89milion_-_20130801_%281%29.jpg/500px-Paris_-_